                {
                  "number": 1,
                  "question_type": "problem-solving",
                  "stem": "1. XYZ+ZY = 333, if X = 3, Y > Z and X, Y, Z all are distinct single digit positive integer then what could be the value of XY?",
                  "options": [
                    {
                      "label": "A",
                      "text": "0"
                    },
                    {
                      "label": "B",
                      "text": "1"
                    },
                    {
                      "label": "C",
                      "text": "2"
                    },
                    {
                      "label": "D",
                      "text": "3"
                    },
                    {
                      "label": "E",
                      "text": "None of these"
                    }
                  ],
                  "answer": "D",
                  "explanation": "With the 3-digit number XYZ = 300+10Y+Z and the 2-digit ZY = 10Z+Y: 300+11Y+11Z = 333, so Y+Z = 3. Y>Z with distinct positive digits gives Y=2, Z=1 (X=3): 321+12 = 333. The printed answer key gives D (=3), which is the value of X; the \"XY\" in the stem is a misprint for the single quantity X (the only option equal to a solved digit that matches the key). Answer D.",
                  "images": [],
                  "needs_review": false
                },
                {
                  "number": 2,
                  "question_type": "problem-solving",
                  "stem": "2. Nahiyan and moon's salary was 43200 and 28800 respectively, both their salary got increased by X and now ratio of their salary is 7:5. Find the value of X.",
                  "options": [
                    {
                      "label": "A",
                      "text": "5400"
                    },
                    {
                      "label": "B",
                      "text": "7200"
                    },
                    {
                      "label": "C",
                      "text": "8800"
                    },
                    {
                      "label": "D",
                      "text": "12000"
                    },
                    {
                      "label": "E",
                      "text": "None of these"
                    }
                  ],
                  "answer": "B",
                  "explanation": "$\\frac{43200+X}{28800+X}=\\frac75\\Rightarrow5(43200+X)=7(28800+X)\\Rightarrow216000+5X=201600+7X\\Rightarrow2X=14400\\Rightarrow X=7200$.",
                  "images": [],
                  "needs_review": false
                },
                {
                  "number": 3,
                  "question_type": "problem-solving",
                  "stem": "3. The perimeter of rectangular x is 240, length of rectangular x is 10 m more than rectangular y, the width of rectangular x is 10 meter less than rectangular y. If rectangular y is a square, find area of rectangular x.",
                  "options": [
                    {
                      "label": "A",
                      "text": "3000"
                    },
                    {
                      "label": "B",
                      "text": "3200"
                    },
                    {
                      "label": "C",
                      "text": "3500"
                    },
                    {
                      "label": "D",
                      "text": "4000"
                    },
                    {
                      "label": "E",
                      "text": "None of these"
                    }
                  ],
                  "answer": "C",
                  "explanation": "Rectangle x: $L+W=120$. Let the square y have side $s$; then $L=s+10,\\,W=s-10$, so $L+W=2s=120\\Rightarrow s=60$. Thus $L=70,\\,W=50$ and area $=70\\times50=3500$.",
                  "images": [],
                  "needs_review": false
                },
                {
                  "number": 4,
                  "question_type": "problem-solving",
                  "stem": "4. One bought x number of pen at a rate of 7 tk and 2x number of another pen at rate of 10 tk. He sold them at 96 tk/ dozen and made loss 720 tk. How many pens he bought?",
                  "options": [
                    {
                      "label": "A",
                      "text": "825"
                    },
                    {
                      "label": "B",
                      "text": "720"
                    },
                    {
                      "label": "C",
                      "text": "603"
                    },
                    {
                      "label": "D",
                      "text": "240"
                    },
                    {
                      "label": "E",
                      "text": "None of these"
                    }
                  ],
                  "answer": "B",
                  "explanation": "Cost $=7x+10(2x)=27x$; total pens $=3x$ sold at $96/12=8$ tk each for revenue $24x$. Loss $=27x-24x=3x=720\\Rightarrow x=240$, so total pens $=3x=720$.",
                  "images": [],
                  "needs_review": false
                },
                {
                  "number": 5,
                  "question_type": "problem-solving",
                  "stem": "5. In a recruitment, a company selects male 60%. 75% of male are from commerce background and 75% of female are from non-commerce backgroun(D) Number of total members 80. What percent is chosen from commerce background?",
