                {
                  "number": 7,
                  "question_type": "problem-solving",
                  "stem": "7. In a group of 1200 people, 80% were women, a certain amount of women left and new percentage of women is 70%, how many women left the group?",
                  "options": [
                    {
                      "label": "A",
                      "text": "200"
                    },
                    {
                      "label": "B",
                      "text": "280"
                    },
                    {
                      "label": "C",
                      "text": "36"
                    },
                    {
                      "label": "D",
                      "text": "400"
                    },
                    {
                      "label": "E",
                      "text": "None of these"
                    }
                  ],
                  "answer": "D",
                  "explanation": "Women $=960$. If $w$ leave: $\\frac{960-w}{1200-w}=0.7\\Rightarrow960-w=840-0.7w\\Rightarrow0.3w=120\\Rightarrow w=400$.",
                  "images": [],
