                {
                  "number": 8,
                  "question_type": "problem-solving",
                  "stem": "8. $(x^{2}+3)$ when divided by 32 and remainder is 7 and if x is a positive integer then which of the following must also be an integer?\ni. $\\frac{x}{2}$    ii. $\\frac{x}{4}$    iii. $\\frac{x}{6}$",
                  "options": [
                    {
                      "label": "A",
                      "text": "i"
                    },
                    {
                      "label": "B",
                      "text": "ii"
                    },
                    {
                      "label": "C",
                      "text": "i & iii"
                    },
                    {
                      "label": "D",
                      "text": "iii"
                    },
                    {
                      "label": "E",
                      "text": "None of these"
                    }
                  ],
                  "answer": "A",
                  "explanation": "$x^{2}+3\\equiv7\\pmod{32}\\Rightarrow x^{2}\\equiv4\\pmod{32}$. The solutions are $x\\equiv2\\pmod4$ (e.g. 2, 6, 10, 14), so $x$ is even and $x/2$ is always an integer, while $x/4$ and $x/6$ are not. Only i.",
                  "images": [],
                  "needs_review": false
                },
                {
                  "number": 9,
                  "question_type": "problem-solving",
                  "stem": "9. If  $3x - 2 \\geq 1$ , what is the least possible value of  $3x + 2$ ?",
                  "options": [
                    {
                      "label": "A",
                      "text": "5"
                    },
                    {
                      "label": "B",
                      "text": "3"
                    },
                    {
                      "label": "C",
                      "text": "2"
                    },
                    {
                      "label": "D",
                      "text": "1"
                    },
                    {
                      "label": "E",
                      "text": "None of these"
                    }
                  ],
                  "answer": "A",
                  "explanation": "$3x-2\\ge1\\Rightarrow3x\\ge3$, so $3x+2\\ge5$; the least value is 5.",
                  "images": [],
                  "needs_review": false
                },
