                  "explanation": "Buying one day later means fewer days in advance and a smaller discount. Crossing the 30-day boundary: at 30 days the 30% discount gives $0.7F=252\\Rightarrow F=360$; at 29 days the 15% discount gives $0.85\\times360=306$. So she bought 30 days in advance.",
